{
  "description": "The cash desk's handover check (cash desk spec, CSH-02, CSH-03, CSH-04, PRD W4, W7): may this cashier confirm this bill now, and what is recorded. A positive cash due is a handover in, a negative one a payout. The cash received is the cashier's correction, else the salesman's figure, else the exact amount; a bill known only from its code has no salesman's figure. Unless a case says otherwise: session …51 is open on this desk for cashier …a5 (a cashier: cash.handover.receive, cash.refund.pay, cash.session.close); …a6 may receive handovers but not pay refunds; …a1 is a salesman. Unit Rs 1 = 100, amounts in paisa. A queue row may say the bill was voided (W1-12): bill_voided, checked right after nothing_to_collect, so the cashier never takes cash for it.",
